[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m user
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m You have seven bags of gold coins. Each bag has the same number of gold coins. One day, you find a bag of 53 coins. You decide to redistribute the number of coins you have so that all eight bags you hold have the same number of coins. You successfully manage to redistribute all the coins, and you also note that you have more than 200 coins. What is the smallest number of coins you could have had before finding the bag of 53 coins?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To solve this problem, let's denote the number of coins in each of the original seven bags as \( x \). The total number of coins before finding the bag of 53 coins is therefore \( 7x \). After finding the bag of 53 coins, the total number of coins becomes \( 7x + 53 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m We need to redistribute these coins so that all eight bags have the same number of coins. This means each of the eight bags should have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \frac{7x + 53}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Since the number of coins in each bag must be an integer, \( 7x + 53 \) must be divisible by 8. We can express this condition as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 7x + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Simplifying the equation modulo 8, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 7x + 53 \equiv x + 5 \equiv 0 \pmod{8} \quad \text{(since } 53 \div 8 = 6 \text{ remainder } 5\text{)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This simplifies further to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m x \equiv -5 \pmod{8} \quad \text{or} \quad x \equiv 3 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m So, \( x \) can be written as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m x = 8k + 3 \quad \text{for some integer } k
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m We are also given that after finding the bag of 53 coins, the total number of coins is more than 200. Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 7x + 53 > 200
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Substituting \( x = 8k + 3 \) into this inequality, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 7(8k + 3) + 53 > 200 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 56k + 21 + 53 > 200 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 56k + 74 > 200 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 56k > 126 \quad \Rightarrow \quad k > \frac{126}{56} \quad \Rightarrow \quad k > 2.25
