[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To find the value of \(x\) given that the arithmetic mean of the numbers 7, 2, \(x\), and 10 is 9, we start with the formula for the arithmetic mean. The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers. Here, we have four numbers: 7, 2, \(x\), and 10. The arithmetic mean of these numbers is given as 9.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m The formula for the arithmetic mean is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m We know the arithmetic mean is 9, so we can set up the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 9 = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m First, we simplify the numerator on the right side of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 9 = \frac{19 + x}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Next, we eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 9 \times 4 = 19 + x
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 36 = 19 + x
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To isolate \(x\), we subtract 19 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 36 - 19 = x
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Thus, the value of \(x\) is \(\boxed{17}\).
