[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To find the value of \( x \) given that the arithmetic mean of 7, 2, \( x \), and 10 is 9, we start by using the definition of the arithmetic mean. The arithmetic mean of four numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by 4. Therefore, we can write the equation for the arithmetic mean as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m First, we simplify the sum in the numerator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \frac{19 + x}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Next, we eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 19 + x = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Now, we solve for \( x \) by isolating it on one side of the equation. We do this by subtracting 19 from both sides:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m x = 36 - 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
