[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m A Senate committee has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats.  In how many ways can we form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party (i.e., at least one Republican and at least one Democrat), we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 members (8 Republicans and 6 Democrats). This can be done using the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) elements from \( n \) elements without regard to order.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5!9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 2. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members consisting only of Republicans. This is the number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5!3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 3. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members consisting only of Democrats. This is the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5!1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 4. Subtract the number of all-Republican subcommittees and all-Democrat subcommittees from the total number of subcommittees to find the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5} = 2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m So, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
