[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To solve this problem, let's denote the original number of coins in each of the seven bags as \( x \). After finding the bag of 53 coins, you redistribute the coins so that all eight bags (seven bags plus the one with 53 coins) have the same number of coins. Let's say this common number of coins in each bag is \( y \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m The total number of coins you have initially is \( 7x \). After adding the 53 coins, you have \( 7x + 53 \) coins. Since these coins are redistributed so that each of the eight bags has \( y \) coins, we can write:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ 7x + 53 = 8y \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This equation tells us that \( 7x + 53 \) must be divisible by 8. We also know that \( y \) must be an integer, so \( 7x + 53 \) must be an integer multiple of 8. This means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ 7x + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ 7x \equiv -53 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ 7x \equiv -53 + 64 \pmod{8} \] (since \(-53 + 64 = 11 \equiv 3 \pmod{8}\))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ 7x \equiv 3 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To solve for \( x \), we need the multiplicative inverse of 7 modulo 8. The inverse of 7 modulo 8 is a number \( z \) such that \( 7z \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \). By testing, we find that \( 7 \times 7 = 49 \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \), so the inverse is 7. Therefore, we can multiply both sides of the congruence by 7:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ x \equiv 3 \times 7 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ x \equiv 21 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ x \equiv 5 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This means \( x = 8k + 5 \) for some integer \( k \). The smallest possible value for \( x \) occurs when \( k = 0 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ x = 5 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Now, we need to check that this value satisfies the condition that you have more than 200 coins after finding the bag of 53 coins. If \( x = 5 \), then the total number of coins is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ 7 \times 5 + 53 = 35 + 53 = 88 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This is not more than 200 coins, so we need to check the next possible value of \( k \), which is \( k = 1 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ x = 8 \times 1 + 5 = 13 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ 7 \times 13 + 53 = 91 + 53 = 144 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This is also not more than 200 coins. We need to check the next possible value of \( k \), which is \( k = 2 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ x = 8 \times 2 + 5 = 21 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ 7 \times 21 + 53 = 147 + 53 = 200 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This is not more than 200 coins. We need to check the next possible value of \( k \), which is \( k = 3 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[ x = 8 \times 3 + 5 = 29 \]
