[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party (Republican and Democrat), we can use the principle of complementary counting. Here are the steps to solve the problem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a total of 14 members (8 Republicans and 6 Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 2. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee with no Democrats (all Republicans):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 3. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee with no Republicans (all Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 4. The number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party is the total number of subcommittees minus the number of subcommittees with all Republicans and the number of subcommittees with all Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5} = 2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
