[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that includes at least one member from each party (8 Republicans and 6 Democrats), we can use the principle of complementary counting. First, we calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 (8 Republicans and 6 Democrats). Then, we subtract the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 2. Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans (and hence no Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 3. Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Democrats (and hence no Republicans):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 4. Add the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans and the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Democrats. These are the ways to form a subcommittee that is missing at least one member from each party:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 5. Subtract the result from step 4 from the total number of ways calculated in step 1 to get the number of ways to form a subcommittee that has at least one member from each party:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m So the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \boxed{1940}
