[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    88 > 200 \text{ (This is not true)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m    Since we need the smallest number of coins and each step provides \( 88 \), it looks correct as \( 7n + 53 = 88 \) and \( 88 \div 8 = 11 \). Thus, \( k = 11 \). Hence the smallest possible initial number of coins per bag is indeed:
