[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with the requirement that the subcommittee must include at least one member from each party, we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 members (8 Republicans and 6 Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 2. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee with all members of one party and none from the other party. This would be two cases:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m     - All Republicans (with at least one Republican):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m     \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m     \text{Ways to choose 5 Republicans out of 8} = \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m     \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m     - All Democrats (with at least one Democrat):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m     \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m     \text{Ways to choose 5 Democrats out of 6} = \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m     \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 3. Add the results of the two cases to find the number of ways that do not satisfy the condition of having at least one member from each party:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
