[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To find the value of \( x \), we start by using the definition of the arithmetic mean. The arithmetic mean of the numbers 7, 2, \( x \), and 10 is given as 9. The formula for the arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers. In this case, we have four numbers, so the formula becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To isolate \( x \), we first multiply both sides of the equation by 4 to clear the fraction:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 7 + 2 + x + 10 = 9 \times 4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 19 + x = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Next, we isolate \( x \) by subtracting 19 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m x = 36 - 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Thus, the value of \( x \) is \(\boxed{17}\).
