[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m input:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m user
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m A Senate committee has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats.  In how many ways can we form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party (Republican and Democrat), we can use the principle of complementary counting.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m First, calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats). This is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Next, we need to subtract the number of ways to choose 5 members that do not meet the condition of having at least one member from each party. There are two cases to consider:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 1. All 5 members are from Republicans (i.e., all 5 Republicans and no Democrats).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 2. All 5 members are from Democrats (i.e., all 5 Democrats and no Republicans).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m For the first case (all Republicans):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m For the second case (all Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m The total number of ways to form a subcommittee with no Democrats or no Republicans is the sum of the above two cases:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
