[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m A Senate committee has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats.  In how many ways can we form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee that has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with the condition that the subcommittee must have at least one member from each party, we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 1. Identify the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 without any restrictions. This is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \(k\) elements from a set of \(n\) elements without regard to the order of selection.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{14}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 2. Calculate the value of \( \binom{14}{5} \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 3. Next, calculate the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with only Republicans or only Democrats. This means we subtract the two cases where all 5 members are either Republicans or Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 4. Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 Republicans out of 8:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 5. Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats out of 6:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = \frac{6}{1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 6. Now subtract the two cases (all Republicans and all Democrats) from the total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5} = 2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \boxed{1940}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2534317)[0m \]
